# hkask-mcp-codegraph

## Single-graph unit tests give false confidence for cross-file features

Cross-file edge resolution and grouped-import parsing both regressed
silently because every unit test indexed a single in-memory graph and
asserted only within-file behavior. The unit suite stayed green while
`codegraph_traverse`/`codegraph_impact` were dropping all cross-file
edges and `extract_import` emitted malformed targets like `"Arc}"`.

Guard: a `tests/` integration test that indexes ≥2 on-disk fixture
files and asserts call/import edge **topology** (caller → callee, which
file the callee lives in). Do not rely on single in-memory-graph unit
tests for resolution or extraction correctness — they cannot exercise
cross-file name resolution or tree-sitter parsing of real `use` trees.
When changing edge resolution (`resolve_target`/`resolve_and_insert_edges`)
or `extract_import`/`collect_use_targets`, extend this integration test
rather than adding another single-graph unit test.